WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.259
A kitchen fire can force a decision before you have time to search for
instructions.

2
00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:09.480
Is it still a small, confined pan fire, or is it time to leave?

3
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:14.345
Knowing a safety rule is different from recognizing the situation in
front of you.

4
00:00:14.485 --> 00:00:17.761
Two Minutes turns that decision into a short practice drill.

5
00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:24.179
The Lens puts a virtual cooktop, lid, burner control and marked exit
into your space.

6
00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:27.806
Two starting conditions let you compare different decisions.

7
00:00:27.946 --> 00:00:29.952
Leaving is available throughout.

8
00:00:30.092 --> 00:00:33.951
This demonstration runs in Lens Studio's preview for Specs.

9
00:00:34.941 --> 00:00:37.438
Here, the fire is confined to the pan.

10
00:00:37.578 --> 00:00:42.559
I lift the lid at the side, slide it over the pan and switch off the
front burner control.

11
00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:48.746
The drill recognizes containment and reminds me to keep the pan
covered until completely cool.

12
00:00:48.886 --> 00:00:53.526
It never forces a correctly contained fire to spread for a dramatic
ending.

13
00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:56.804
If I have any doubt, leaving is still the right option.

14
00:00:57.794 --> 00:01:01.656
In the second scenario, the fire has already spread beyond the pan.

15
00:01:01.796 --> 00:01:04.359
Approaching the lid or burner cannot solve it.

16
00:01:04.499 --> 00:01:07.689
I turn toward the virtual exit and choose to leave.

17
00:01:07.829 --> 00:01:12.809
Outside in the drill, I can close the door when safe and simulate
calling for help.

18
00:01:12.949 --> 00:01:15.182
Leaving does not extinguish the fire.

19
00:01:15.322 --> 00:01:17.245
The next action is to stay out.

20
00:01:18.235 --> 00:01:21.075
Water is an unsafe choice for a grease fire.

21
00:01:21.215 --> 00:01:26.328
Selecting the virtual glass triggers a restrained consequence and an
evacuation path.

22
00:01:26.468 --> 00:01:28.413
I leave and call from outside.

23
00:01:28.553 --> 00:01:34.249
The debrief explains why water was unsafe and records both the mistake
and the recovery.

24
00:01:34.389 --> 00:01:36.632
A reset clears the previous attempt.

25
00:01:37.622 --> 00:01:39.493
Planning used Devpost Learn.

26
00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:43.836
The build uses CLAD, Lens Studio and the Lens Studio MCP.

27
00:01:43.976 --> 00:01:50.568
SIK handles interaction, UIKit handles the views and one state machine
owns every decision.

28
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:54.897
Twenty-three portable tests and seven native preview cases passed.

29
00:01:55.887 --> 00:01:58.012
The kitchen and exit are virtual.

30
00:01:58.152 --> 00:02:02.141
Real-glasses comfort and teaching effectiveness still need testing.

31
00:02:02.281 --> 00:02:06.442
Two Minutes names the drill, not a safe amount of time to stay in a
fire.
